{"id":"0597127ba0cc6437","group":"58","path":"58/batch11/58-df-utility.md","title":"Utility Function","display":"df-utility — Utility Function","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-utility","aliases":["58-df-utility","Utility Function"],"display":"df-utility — Utility Function","depends_on":["[[../batch12/58-df-preference.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-utility"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-utility</span><span>Utility Function</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-utility — Utility Function"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e7154db810649ee7\" href=\"?note=e7154db810649ee7\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-preference.md\">../batch12/58-df-preference.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> (consumption set, usually <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}_+^n\">\\(\\mathbb{R}_+^n\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\succsim\">\\(\\succsim\\)</span> (preference relation on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"u: X \\to \\mathbb{R}\">\\(u: X \\to \\mathbb{R}\\)</span> (utility function)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Preference}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Preference}_S\\)</span> (complete-transitive preference predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"e7154db810649ee7\" href=\"?note=e7154db810649ee7\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-preference.md\">../batch12/58-df-preference.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{UtilityRepresentation}_S,\\mathrm{StrictlyIncreasingUtility}_S,\\mathrm{QuasiconcaveUtility}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{UtilityRepresentation}_S,\\mathrm{StrictlyIncreasingUtility}_S,\\mathrm{QuasiconcaveUtility}_S\\)</span> (utility predicates defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}utility} \\vdash \\mathrm{UtilityRepresentation}_S(u,\\succsim,X)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Preference}_S(X,\\succsim)\\land u:X\\to\\mathbb R\\land \\forall x,y\\in X\\;(x\\succsim y\\leftrightarrow u(x)\\geq u(y))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}utility} \\vdash \\mathrm{UtilityRepresentation}_S(u,\\succsim,X)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Preference}_S(X,\\succsim)\\land u:X\\to\\mathbb R\\land \\forall x,y\\in X\\;(x\\succsim y\\leftrightarrow u(x)\\geq u(y))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}utility} \\vdash \\mathrm{StrictlyIncreasingUtility}_S(u,X,n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\\land X\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n_+\\land u:X\\to\\mathbb R\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\bigl((\\forall i\\in n\\;x_i\\geq y_i)\\land x\\neq y\\to u(x)&gt;u(y)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}utility} \\vdash \\mathrm{StrictlyIncreasingUtility}_S(u,X,n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\\land X\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n_+\\land u:X\\to\\mathbb R\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\bigl((\\forall i\\in n\\;x_i\\geq y_i)\\land x\\neq y\\to u(x)&gt;u(y)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}utility} \\vdash \\mathrm{QuasiconcaveUtility}_S(u,X,n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\\land X\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\land u:X\\to\\mathbb R\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\forall\\lambda\\in[0,1]\\;\\bigl(\\lambda x+(1-\\lambda)y\\in X\\to u(\\lambda x+(1-\\lambda)y)\\geq\\min\\{u(x),u(y)\\}\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}utility} \\vdash \\mathrm{QuasiconcaveUtility}_S(u,X,n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\mathbb N_{&gt;0}\\land X\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\land u:X\\to\\mathbb R\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\forall\\lambda\\in[0,1]\\;\\bigl(\\lambda x+(1-\\lambda)y\\in X\\to u(\\lambda x+(1-\\lambda)y)\\geq\\min\\{u(x),u(y)\\}\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The first assertion defines representation only; existence of such a function requires additional hypotheses on the preference and domain.</li>\n<li>Coordinates of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\mathbb R^n\\)</span> are indexed by the finite ordinal <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n=\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}\">\\(n=\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}\\)</span>; the former bound <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"i\\leq n\">\\(i\\leq n\\)</span> included a nonexistent <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(n+1)\">\\((n+1)\\)</span>-st coordinate.</li>\n<li>Ordinal utility: unique up to monotone transformation; only ordering matters</li>\n<li>Cardinal utility: affine transformations allowed; measurable utility in expected utility</li>\n<li>Expected utility: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"u(w) = \\sum p_i u(w_i)\">\\(u(w) = \\sum p_i u(w_i)\\)</span> for gamble <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{(p_i, w_i)\\}\">\\(\\{(p_i, w_i)\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li>St. Petersburg paradox: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E[u] = \\sum \\frac{1}{n}\">\\(E[u] = \\sum \\frac{1}{n}\\)</span> diverges; resolves via risk aversion</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Mas-Colell, Whinston and Green, Microeconomic Theory</li>\n<li>Kreps, Notes on the Theory of Choice</li>\n<li>Fishburn, Utility Theory for Decision Making</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch12/58-df-preference.md","status":"resolved","id":"e7154db810649ee7","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-preference.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-preference.md","status":"resolved","id":"e7154db810649ee7","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Preference}_S$ (complete-transitive preference predicate, see [[../batch12/58-df-preference.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb{R}_+^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\succsim","display":false},{"tex":"X","display":false},{"tex":"u: X \\to \\mathbb{R}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Preference}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{UtilityRepresentation}_S,\\mathrm{StrictlyIncreasingUtility}_S,\\mathrm{QuasiconcaveUtility}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}utility} \\vdash \\mathrm{UtilityRepresentation}_S(u,\\succsim,X)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Preference}_S(X,\\succsim)\\land u:X\\to\\mathbb R\\land \\forall x,y\\in X\\;(x\\succsim y\\leftrightarrow u(x)\\geq u(y))","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}utility} \\vdash \\mathrm{StrictlyIncreasingUtility}_S(u,X,n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\mathbb N_{>0}\\land X\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n_+\\land u:X\\to\\mathbb R\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\bigl((\\forall i\\in n\\;x_i\\geq y_i)\\land x\\neq y\\to u(x)>u(y)\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}utility} \\vdash \\mathrm{QuasiconcaveUtility}_S(u,X,n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\mathbb N_{>0}\\land X\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\land u:X\\to\\mathbb R\\land\\forall x,y\\in X\\;\\forall\\lambda\\in[0,1]\\;\\bigl(\\lambda x+(1-\\lambda)y\\in X\\to u(\\lambda x+(1-\\lambda)y)\\geq\\min\\{u(x),u(y)\\}\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathbb R^n","display":false},{"tex":"n=\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"i\\leq n","display":false},{"tex":"(n+1)","display":false},{"tex":"u(w) = \\sum p_i u(w_i)","display":false},{"tex":"\\{(p_i, w_i)\\}","display":false},{"tex":"E[u] = \\sum \\frac{1}{n}","display":false}],"bytes":2324,"backlinks":[{"id":"d67f64f2aefcc752","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$u:\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}^n\\to\\mathbb R$ (效用函数, see [[../batch11/58-df-utility.md]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1359","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-utility.md|58-df-utility]]（batch11）"}],"outgoing":["e7154db810649ee7","36d7463d215be751"]}